WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:10.160
In June 2021, the Office of the Director of&nbsp;
National Intelligence issued its long-awaited

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:15.920
report on unidentified aerial phenomena. Pollsters&nbsp;
have been asking Americans about UFOs since the

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:21.600
early 1970s and the public has long been skeptical&nbsp;
about what the government knows about them.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:26.960
A quarter century ago, 71% told Gallup the&nbsp;
government knew more than it was telling us.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:33.873
This summer, before the government's report came&nbsp;out,
65% echoed that sentiment in an Economist/YouGov poll.

00:00:33.873 --> 00:00:39.751
11% said the government had&nbsp;told the public
everything it knows and 24% weren't sure.

00:00:39.751 --> 00:00:44.160
The government found no evidence that the&nbsp;
aerial phenomena seen in recent years were alien

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:50.000
spacecraft, but they couldn't explain what is going&nbsp;
on up in the atmosphere. In a Gallup question

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:56.240
asked after the report came out, 41% said that&nbsp;
they believe some UFOs have been extraterrestrial

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:02.480
spacecraft, while 50% said all sightings could be&nbsp;
explained by human activity or natural phenomena.

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:08.197
It's clear that the government's report hasn't&nbsp;
dampened public interest in UFOs.

00:01:08.197 --> 00:01:13.965
Have you ever seen a UFO? Let us know in our poll.
Also, let us&nbsp;know what other topics you'd like

00:01:13.965 --> 00:01:20.880
our scholars to cover in 60 seconds, and be sure to like
and&nbsp;subscribe for more research and videos from AEI.

